<VI _name="RemoteVI Arrange Controls.vi" description="Lays out a running VI's own front panel (the RemoteVI UIs arrange themselves when they start\3A AIXML has no panel layout)\3A every top-level control whose label is in layout is moved to left\2C top (Position\2C label included) and sized to width\2C height where LabVIEW lets a running VI resize it (a boolean\3A Button Size\3B a string\3A Size\3B a multicolumn listbox\3A as many rows as fit into height - 0 keeps the size)\3B a NEGATIVE width hides the control instead (Visible FALSE\3B the RemoteVI UIs hide their tick and stop controls so)\3B the window gets title and a panel area of panel size (Front Panel Window\3APanel Bounds\2C its top-left kept). A boolean shows its label as its boolean text (centred) instead of beside it\2C so it looks like a labelled button. Controls not in layout are left where they are. The tool bar\2C menu bar and scroll bars are hidden (where LabVIEW allows it while the VI runs). Errors of the property writes are ignored\3B the panel still opens.">
